3. Signal key-transparency-server (Key Transparency log package, Go)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Upstream:      https://github.com/signalapp/key-transparency-server
Pinned commit: 30b7a2a40604fbe04545d47f26e4c5a35f5d3161  (2026-08-18, "Update go to 1.26.6")
License:       AGPL-3.0-only (upstream `LICENSE`)

How NYX uses it (unmodified upstream packages):
  * `server/kt-query/vendor/github.com/signalapp/keytransparency/` — the pinned
    upstream module, generated by `go mod vendor` (the module is private and cannot
    be fetched over the network). The committed `server/kt-query/go.mod` therefore
    carries **no** `replace` directive and builds with `-mod=vendor`, offline.
    `server/kt-query/build.sh` refuses to build if `vendor/` is missing; setting
    `NYX_KT_UPSTREAM=/path/to/key-transparency-server` temporarily switches to a
    local checkout (pin-chasing only).
  * `server/kt-query/` — thin Go services that own the local LevelDB logs and
    serve NYX's read and write paths. Since the v1 retirement (`docs/38`) only the
    v2 log remains: `cmd/nyx-kt-query-v2` (log), `cmd/nyx-kt-auditor-v2` (auditor,
    §4), and `cmd/nyx-kt-v2-init` (bootstrap). They are not a distribution of the
    upstream *server* binary: only library packages (`tree/transparency` fork in
    `v2/transparency`, `db`, protobuf) are vendored and linked into our own
    services.
  * Server-side proxy/metrics: `server/src/routes/ktQuery.ts`; log writer:
    `server/src/utils/keyTransparency.ts` (`docs/32`).

