Notes for redistribution
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Because the pinned upstream sources are AGPL-3.0, every distributed copy of the
  compiled artifacts above (`packages/spqr-wasm/dist/spqr.wasm`) and of the
  `nyx-kt-query-v2` binary is a distribution of AGPL-3.0 code. The same applies to
  the `nyx-kt-auditor-v2` binary, which contains the Go port of §4 (AGPL-3.0).
  Corresponding source is the upstream repository at the pinned commit listed above
  (plus this repository's thin wrappers).
* Rebuilding the artifacts needs no external checkout: the pinned sources are in
  `vendor/signal/` and `server/kt-query/vendor/` (see each `build.sh` and
  `README.md`). CI builds the v2 log from the vendored module **and rebuilds the
  WASM artifacts** on every push, comparing their SHA-256 against
  `packages/wasm-artifacts.json` (`scripts/wasm-repro-build.sh --verify`, job
  `wasm`). That is the correspondence proof for the AGPL binaries shipped in
  `packages/*/dist/`: the committed `.wasm` files are byte-identical to what the
  pinned sources in this repository produce with the pinned toolchain
  (`1.95.0`, `packages/*/rust-toolchain.toml`), built at the canonical root
  `/tmp/nyx-wasm-repro` (cargo's unit hash embeds the package path, so the build
  directory has to be fixed — see the long comment in `scripts/wasm-repro-build.sh`).
* Keep this file together with `LICENSE` in any redistribution.

Pins are recorded here and in `docs/30` §30.2; repository layout and root-policy
files are catalogued in `docs/25`.
